<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2" xmlns:gx="http://www.google.com/kml/ext/2.2" xmlns:kml="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
<Document>
	<name>Maine Lake Depths</name>
	<open>1</open>
	<description>LakeDpth consolidates several sources of lake depth sample information. Each point indicates the depth of the lake at that location, along with the surface elevation of the lake. The data can be used to map the lake beds or compute lake volumes. The data sources used in this layer differ in their accuracy and are coded so the user can relate a certain level of confidence to each point. Data sources include points digitized off Dept. of Inland Fisheries and Wildlife lake depth maps and elevations determined by combination GPS/depthfinder equipment. Some lakes will have points from multiple sources. Users should consult the feature-level metadata fields to determine which points are appropriate for their work and select them out using a definition query.
         http://geolibportal.usm.maine.edu/geonetwork/srv/en/metadata.show?id=345</description>
	<LookAt>
